sentences.text:
[4.0] Learned advocate Ms. Aman A. Shaikh for the original complainant appearing through Legal Aid Committee as well as the learned APP appearing on behalf of the respondent-State have opposed the present application and requested to dismiss the present application for regular bail on the ground that present applicant happens to be the father in law of the deceased who was minor and the son of the applicant married with the minor girl and committed offence of rape and thereafter due to discord in marriage life, alleged incident took place wherein the son of the applicant set ablaze the deceased, who was pregnant and the present applicant gave pregnancy termination pills to the deceased while she was admitted in hospital for treatment of burn injuries and the dying declaration of deceased was also record and hence, there being prima facie involvement of the present applicant, they have requested to dismiss the present application.
[5.0] While granting bail, the Court has to consider the involvement of the accused in the alleged offence, the jurisdiction to grant bail has to be exercised on the basis of the well settled principles having regard to the facts and circumstances of each case and the following factors are to be taken into consideration while considering an application for bail: (i) the nature of accusation and the severity of the punishment and the nature of the materials relied upon by the prosecution; (ii)
reasonable apprehension of tampering with the witnesses and threat to the complainant or the NEUTRAL CITATION R/CR.MA/17544/2024 ORDER DATED: 12/12/2024 undefined witnesses;
(iii) reasonable possibility of securing the presence of the accused at the time of trial or the likelihood of his abscondence;
(iv) character behaviour and standing of the accused and the circumstances which are peculiar to the accused; (v) larger interest of the public or the State and similar other considerations are required to be considered.

Following aspects have been considered:
(1) Investigation is over and charge-sheet is filed;
(2) The role attributed to the present applicant is that he is the father in law of the deceased and administered pregnancy termination pills to the deceased while she was admitted in the hospital for treatment of burn injuries after she was set at ablaze by the son of the applicant after sprinkling petrol on her.

(3) None of the offence alleged is punishable with life sentence or death penalty;
